# Exercises for coding interviews
## Introduction
In this repository you will find the exercises for the coding interviews.
For each exercise we provide a set of unit tests that you must implement to complete the exercise.
The unit tests in this repository are written with [Jest](https://jestjs.io/).

## How to run tests
1. `npm install`
2. `npm test exercise-name`

## How to use the exercises
First you must create the exercise folder in the `exercises` folder:
```
exercises
├── exercise-name
│   ├── exercise-name.js
│   └── __tests__
│       ├── __tests__.js
│       └── exercise-name.spec.js
```

In the `__tests__` folder you must create `__tests__.js` and `exercise-name.spec.js`
The `__tests__.js` is the source code of your exercise.
The `exercise-name.spec.js` is a test that you must write to test your code.

## How to create an exercise
1. In your `exercises` folder create a new folder with the name of your exercise.
2. In your new folder create the file `exercise-name.js` and the file `__tests__`.
3. In the `exercise-name.js` file write your exercise source code.
4. In the `__tests__` folder create the file `exercise-name.spec.js`.

In the `exercise-name.spec.js` file write your tests. For more information on how to write tests please see the [Jest documentation](https://jestjs.io/).

## Example for writing tests
This example tests the `sumNums` function in the `is-prime` exercise.
```javascript
// __tests__/is-prime.spec.js
import isPrime from "../exercise-name";

describe("is-prime", () => {
  it("returns true when given 2", () => {
    expect(isPrime(2)).toEqual(true);
  });

  it("returns false when given 4", () => {
    expect(isPrime(4)).toEqual(false);
  });
});
