# VulnScout

This python script is used to assist in the identification of vulnerable code snippets in Java.

It takes a set of example code snippets and creates an in-memory database of vulnerable code. It uses an in-memory database to identify any vulnerable code and output the code snippet.

## Setup

This script requires Python 3 and the in-memory database SQLite3.
```
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

## Run

To run the script, use the following command:

```
python main.py
```

You will be prompted to enter the input file:

```
Input Filename:
```

Enter the path to the file that contains the examples. If you do not have any examples, select "test.py" from the "examples" directory.

You will be prompted to enter the output file:

```
Output Filename:
```

Enter the path to the file that you want to write the output to.

## Examples

The examples directory contains example code snippets. You can use these as input to the script.

## Output

The script outputs the vulnerable code in the output file.

